        "date": "2026-11-19T06:23:58Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(machine): judge only the quarter points that an arc sweeps\n\nThe travel check added all four quarter points of an arc's full circle.\nA shallow arc of a large radius (22 m, 0.26 degrees) was then judged\n22 m away from the tool, and a legal 2D Contour did not post on any\nmachine size.\n\nmove_extremes now adds a quarter point only when the sweep from `from`\nto `to`, in `arc.ccw`'s direction and in the arc's plane, passes it.\nAll four stay when the endpoints can post as one point (a full circle\non the control) or the sweep reads zero. The radius is the larger\nendpoint radius.\n\nPinned by crates/app/tests/machine_arc_sweep.rs.\n\nFixes #2710\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
